---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Percentage Formulas & Rechenweg Guide: Complete Math Cheat Sheet"
  description="Master percentage math with full formulas, step-by-step Rechenweg explanations, printable cheat sheet, and real-life examples."
  canonicalUrl="https://prozentrechner-online.com/percentage-formula"
>
  <!-- Header -->
  <div class="mb-10 text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <nav class="flex items-center justify-center gap-2 text-xs font-semibold mb-3" style="color: var(--text-muted);">
      <a href="/" class="hover:underline">Home</a>
      <span>&rsaquo;</span>
      <span style="color: var(--text-ink);">Percentage Formulas & Guide</span>
    </nav>

    <h1 class="font-display font-black text-3xl sm:text-5xl tracking-tight mb-4" style="color: var(--text-ink);">
      Percentage Formulas & <br/>
      <span style="color: var(--accent);">Calculation Steps (Rechenweg)</span>
    </h1>

    <p class="text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--text-muted);">
      Your complete reference guide to percentage calculations: mathematical definitions, step-by-step formulas, printable cheat sheets, and practical examples.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="space-y-12 max-w-4xl mx-auto">
    <!-- 1. The 3 Core Percentage Terms -->
    <section class="rounded-3xl border p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-sm space-y-4" style="background-color: var(--bg-surface); border-color: var(--border-hairline);">
      <h2 class="font-display font-extrabold text-xl sm:text-2xl" style="color: var(--text-ink);">
        1. The Three Fundamental Terms
      </h2>
      <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--text-muted);">
        Every percentage calculation connects three fundamental quantities:
      </p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 text-xs sm:text-sm">
        <div class="p-4 rounded-2xl border space-y-2" style="background-color: var(--bg-surface-soft); border-color: var(--border-hairline);">
          <div class="font-bold text-base" style="color: var(--text-ink);">Base Value (<span class="text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400 font-mono">G</span>)</div>
          <p style="color: var(--text-muted);">The total 100% whole amount.</p>
          <div class="text-[11px] font-mono opacity-80">e.g., A total class of 30 students.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 rounded-2xl border space-y-2" style="background-color: var(--bg-surface-soft); border-color: var(--border-hairline);">
          <div class="font-bold text-base" style="color: var(--text-ink);">Percentage Rate (<span class="text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-400 font-mono">p%</span>)</div>
          <p style="color: var(--text-muted);">The ratio per hundred (number with the % sign).</p>
          <div class="text-[11px] font-mono opacity-80">e.g., 20% of the class.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 rounded-2xl border space-y-2" style="background-color: var(--bg-surface-soft); border-color: var(--border-hairline);">
          <div class="font-bold text-base" style="color: var(--text-ink);">Percentage Value (<span class="text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 font-mono">W</span>)</div>
          <p style="color: var(--text-muted);">The concrete portion or yield amount.</p>
          <div class="text-[11px] font-mono opacity-80">e.g., 6 students (which is 20% of 30).</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 2. Master Formulas Table -->
    <section class="rounded-3xl border p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-sm space-y-6" style="background-color: var(--bg-surface); border-color: var(--border-hairline);">
      <h2 class="font-display font-extrabold text-xl sm:text-2xl" style="color: var(--text-ink);">
        2. Master Formulas Cheat Sheet
      </h2>

      <div class="overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="w-full text-left text-xs sm:text-sm border-collapse">
          <thead>
            <tr class="border-b" style="border-color: var(--border-hairline); color: var(--text-muted);">
              <th class="py-3 px-3 font-bold uppercase tracking-wider">What You Want to Find</th>
              <th class="py-3 px-3 font-bold uppercase tracking-wider">Mathematical Formula</th>
              <th class="py-3 px-3 font-bold uppercase tracking-wider">Example</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y" style="border-color: var(--border-hairline);">
            <tr>
              <td class="py-3.5 px-3 font-bold" style="color: var(--text-ink);">Percentage Value (W)</td>
              <td class="py-3.5 px-3 font-mono font-bold text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400">W = (G &times; p) &divide; 100</td>
              <td class="py-3.5 px-3 font-mono" style="color: var(--text-body);">(200 &times; 15) &divide; 100 = <strong>30</strong></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="py-3.5 px-3 font-bold" style="color: var(--text-ink);">Percentage Rate (p)</td>
              <td class="py-3.5 px-3 font-mono font-bold text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-400">p = (W &divide; G) &times; 100</td>
              <td class="py-3.5 px-3 font-mono" style="color: var(--text-body);">(30 &divide; 200) &times; 100 = <strong>15%</strong></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="py-3.5 px-3 font-bold" style="color: var(--text-ink);">Base Value (G)</td>
              <td class="py-3.5 px-3 font-mono font-bold text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400">G = (W &times; 100) &divide; p</td>
              <td class="py-3.5 px-3 font-mono" style="color: var(--text-body);">(30 &times; 100) &divide; 15 = <strong>200</strong></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="py-3.5 px-3 font-bold" style="color: var(--text-ink);">Percentage Change</td>
              <td class="py-3.5 px-3 font-mono font-bold text-pink-600 dark:text-pink-400">((New &minus; Old) &divide; Old) &times; 100</td>
              <td class="py-3.5 px-3 font-mono" style="color: var(--text-body);">((150 &minus; 100) &divide; 100) &times; 100 = <strong>+50%</strong></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="py-3.5 px-3 font-bold" style="color: var(--text-ink);">Add / Markup %</td>
              <td class="py-3.5 px-3 font-mono font-bold text-teal-600 dark:text-teal-400">V &times; (1 + p &divide; 100)</td>
              <td class="py-3.5 px-3 font-mono" style="color: var(--text-body);">100 &times; (1 + 0.19) = <strong>119</strong></td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 3. The VAT Trap -->
    <section id="vat-trap" class="rounded-3xl border p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-sm space-y-4" style="background-color: var(--bg-surface); border-color: var(--border-hairline);">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider bg-red-100 dark:bg-red-950 text-red-600 dark:text-red-400">
        ⚠️ Critical Math Pitfall
      </div>
      <h2 class="font-display font-extrabold text-xl sm:text-2xl" style="color: var(--text-ink);">
        The VAT Trap: Why +19% then -19% is Wrong
      </h2>
      <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--text-muted);">
        A very common mistake in daily financial calculations is assuming that adding 19% VAT to a price and then subtracting 19% brings you back to the original price.
      </p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 text-xs sm:text-sm pt-2">
        <div class="p-4 rounded-2xl border border-red-200 dark:border-red-900 bg-red-50/50 dark:bg-red-950/30 space-y-1.5">
          <div class="font-bold text-red-600 dark:text-red-400">❌ The False Assumption:</div>
          <div>1. Net: $100.00</div>
          <div>2. Add 19%: $100 + $19 = $119.00 (Gross)</div>
          <div>3. Subtract 19% of $119: $119 &minus; $22.61 = <strong>$96.39</strong> (You lost $3.61!)</div>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 rounded-2xl border border-emerald-200 dark:border-emerald-900 bg-emerald-50/50 dark:bg-emerald-950/30 space-y-1.5">
          <div class="font-bold text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400">✅ The Correct Rechenweg:</div>
          <div>1. Gross Total: $119.00</div>
          <div>2. Divide by (1 + 0.19) = 1.19</div>
          <div>3. Correct Net: $119.00 &divide; 1.19 = <strong>$100.00</strong></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Quick Jump CTA -->
    <div class="text-center py-6">
      <a
        href="/#main-calc"
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 rounded-2xl font-bold text-sm shadow-md hover:scale-105 transition-all cursor-pointer"
        style="background-color: var(--brand-primary); color: var(--brand-primary-text);"
      >
        <span>⚡ Open Instant Percentage Calculator</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
